>Hmm.. at school I was taught that "belonging to her" is "her".

Depending on location in the sentence. If the possessive precedes the
noun (used as a modifier), it is "her" (e.g. "her house", "her name").
If it follows the noun (used as a pronoun), "hers" is used (e.g. "Is
this computer hers?")

...which partly explains why I'm glad I started with English, rather
than learning it after some other more logical language.

